Build 1.2.5 - 2026-08-15 (SECOND CUT) - ONE FUNNEL, AND THE THREE GATES

Cut from main after the post screen was collapsed onto the one card component.
typecheck clean, 1,821 tests green, production build clean, `npm ci` clean from
an empty checkout, `bun install --frozen-lockfile` clean, website live and
verified serving this code.

WHY THIS REPLACES #90

Build #90 was green and I told the owner to hold it, because it still carried
the fault he found himself: a post opened from the wall rendered a SECOND,
older implementation of the card. Same post, two renderers. That is fixed here
and #90 must not be promoted.

WHAT CHANGED SINCE #90

- `PostDetail` no longer draws its own copy of the post. It renders the same
  `PostCard` the feed and the wall render. One funnel. Its duplicated header
  (the member's name and avatar appeared TWICE) and a wrapper that sliced 16px
  off the card's left edge are gone with it.

- THREE GATES now make today's failures impossible to repeat:
    1. No file outside `src/components/post/` may draw the reaction control or
       the reach/views figures. A second post card cannot be committed.
    2. Any NEW screen that draws engagement fails the tests until somebody
       rules on it in writing. Owner ruled "keep separate" for stories, adverts,
       competition entries, lightboxes, journal and photo library — recorded in
       the gate with the reason and the date.
    3. Both lockfiles must agree with package.json. The stale `bun.lock` that
       stopped the WEBSITE deploying for nine hours can no longer be committed.

EVERYTHING FROM #90 IS STILL HERE

The rebuilt composer, reach/views on the photograph (hover on web, FIRST TAP in
the app), per-reaction icons with counts on the right, the caption that can
break a long word, and the wall's delete animation that finally runs.

WHAT TO CHECK ON THE PHONE - only your device can answer these

  1. Open a post FROM YOUR WALL and from the FEED. They must look identical -
     same header, same icons, same row, same reactions on the right. This is
     the one that was wrong.
  2. Tap a photo ONCE: reach/viewed appears and nothing opens. Tap again: it
     opens.
  3. Double-tap a photo: it likes, and the viewer does NOT open.
  4. Post a photo. Reorder, crop, remove one. The preview must match what is
     published.
  5. Delete one of your own posts: it fades, it does not vanish.
  6. Scroll the feed hard and back: no blank cards, no row shifting under your
     thumb.

NOT DONE, AND NOT CLAIMED

- 12 findings from the screenshot sweep remain open: controls under the 44px
  tap minimum on feed, wall, post and settings, and one avatar that does not
  decode. They are NOT new - they predate today - but they are in this build.
- react-day-picker is still v8, held by `.npmrc`. The cure is v9.
- 38 test files still carry a comment stripper that can delete real code. A
  script was written to fix them and DELIBERATELY REVERTED: removing the
  stripper makes those tests read the file with its comments, so they can pass
  by matching their own explanation. It has to be done one file at a time.

Then promote the AAB.
